  "body": "At one exterior point of the registered Einstein\u2013scalar shell model, enclose the actual total tensor metric coefficient and all first and second coordinate derivatives. The value and scaled time derivative are strictly negative; all three second-derivative signs remain inconclusive at the declared maximum budget. The new value enclosure is a strict subset of the frozen earlier bound.\n\nThe complete 78-term tensor source needs gauge C3 and master C2 after radial differentiation. A differentiated triangular resolvent retains actual input errors, coefficient derivative cross-couplings and all scalar feedback. The frozen source capsule, matching ZIP, external pins and portable replay include independent exact source/geometry/resolvent/coordinate-conversion reviews. Additive English/Spanish site and README entries preserve previous content and frozen manuscripts.\n\nFresh packaged validation passed 16 positive isolated runs, 4 reason-checked expected wrong-formula failures, 17 canonical byte comparisons, 7 source-integrity corruption controls and 9 complete dependency closures unchanged. Normal/optimized scientific outputs agree, including relocated code/repository paths. Full old-tree preservation and subsequent CI/readback are reviewed separately.\n\nThese are conditional ordinary derivatives of a registered-gauge formal coefficient. No covariant curvature, physical gravitational-wave observable, full-domain C2 Einstein residual, finite-amplitude nonlinear family, cosmological origin or novelty claim is established. No new Zenodo version or journal submission accompanies this checkpoint. Private editorial history is excluded.\n",
